\paragraph{SCS as a proxy for conceptual overlap.}
SCS likely functions as a proxy for deeper conceptual overlap between types, rather than as a direct causal mechanism. The renaming experiment (Appendix~\ref{app:renaming}) supports this interpretation: reducing surface-level embedding similarity by 0.20 did not reduce confusion, suggesting that the underlying conceptual similarity persists regardless of label choice. SCS remains practically useful as a lightweight, pre-hoc diagnostic precisely because it correlates with this deeper overlap.

